### ==============================================================================
### StockSync - Microservices Security & Role-Based Authorization Demo
### Delivery 2 Technical Evaluation & Video Recording Script
### ==============================================================================
### This HTTP file contains all requests for the 8 required evaluation scenarios.
### You can run this directly in VS Code (REST Client extension) or JetBrains Rider,
### or import the endpoints into Postman / ThunderClient.

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:9090
@identityUrl = http://localhost:5002
@inventoryUrl = http://localhost:5001
@ordersUrl = http://localhost:5003
@reportingUrl = http://localhost:5004
@notificationUrl = http://localhost:5005

@defaultTenantId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 1: Execution of the Microservices
### Requirement: Show that all microservices and API Gateway are running healthy.
### ==============================================================================

# 1.1 API Gateway Health Check (Gateway + Proxy status)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

# 1.2 Identity Service Swagger JSON / Health
GET {{identityUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json

###

# 1.3 Inventory Service Swagger JSON
GET {{inventoryUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json

###

# 1.4 Orders Service Swagger JSON
GET {{ordersUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json

###

# 1.5 Reporting Service Swagger JSON
GET {{reportingUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json

###

# 1.6 Notification Service Swagger JSON
GET {{notificationUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 2: Identity Initialization via Seeders
### Requirement: Evidentiate creation of users and roles via Seeders (no manual CRUD).
### Seeder initializes:
###  - Tenant: StockSync Demo Store (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)
###  - User 1: owner@stocksync.demo (Role: Owner)
###  - User 2: employee@stocksync.demo (Role: Employee)
### Note for video: Show docker compose logs or run the login endpoints below.
### ==============================================================================


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 3: Authentication and JWT Issuance
### Requirement: Log in with valid credentials and display the generated JWT token.
### ==============================================================================

# 3.1 Login as Owner (Role: Owner)
# @name loginOwner
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@stocksync.demo",
  "password": "Owner123!*",
  "tenantId": "{{defaultTenantId}}"
}

### Store Owner Token from response
@ownerToken = {{loginOwner.response.body.token}}


### 3.2 Login as Employee (Role: Employee)
# @name loginEmployee
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee@stocksync.demo",
  "password": "Employee123!*",
  "tenantId": "{{defaultTenantId}}"
}

### Store Employee Token from response
@employeeToken = {{loginEmployee.response.body.token}}


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 4: Access Without Token (Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
### Requirement: Attempt to consume protected endpoints without JWT and show HTTP 401.
### ==============================================================================

# 4.1 Consume Inventory Service protected endpoint without token
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

###

# 4.2 Consume Orders Service protected endpoint without token
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/orders
Accept: application/json

###

# 4.3 Consume Reporting Service protected endpoint without token
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/reports/sales/summary
Accept: application/json

###

# 4.4 Consume Notification Service protected endpoint without token
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/notifications
Accept: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 5: Access With Valid Token (Expected: HTTP 200 OK)
### Requirement: Consume protected endpoint with a valid JWT and verify access.
### ==============================================================================

# 5.1 List products using valid Owner JWT
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# 5.2 List products using valid Employee JWT
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# 5.3 List orders using valid Owner JWT
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# 5.4 View notifications using valid token
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# 5.5 View sales reports using valid Owner JWT
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/reports/sales/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Accept: application/json


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 6: Role-Based Authorization - With Required Role (Expected: HTTP 201 / 200)
### Requirement: Demonstrate that a user with the required role (Owner) can perform
### restricted management actions (Create product, Create Purchase Order).
### ==============================================================================

# 6.1 Owner creates a new product (Allowed for Role: Owner)
# @name createProductAsOwner
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard Pro RGB",
  "sku": "KB-RGB-DEMO-01",
  "description": "High-end mechanical keyboard for demo",
  "purchasePrice": 45.00,
  "salePrice": 89.99,
  "stockMinimo": 10
}

###

# 6.2 Owner creates a purchase order (Allowed for Role: Owner)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branchId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "supplier": "Logitech Supplies Global",
  "reference": "PO-DEMO-2026-001"
}

###

# 6.3 Owner adds a notification recipient (Allowed for Role: Owner)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/notifications/recipients
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Warehouse Manager Alerts",
  "email": "warehouse@stocksync.demo",
  "phone": "+573001234567",
  "preferredChannel": "Email"
}


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 7: Role-Based Authorization - Without Required Role (Expected: HTTP 403 Forbidden)
### Requirement: Demonstrate that an authenticated user without the required role (Employee)
### receives HTTP 403 Forbidden when trying to perform Owner-only operations.
### ==============================================================================

# 7.1 Employee attempts to create a product (Denied -> HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unauthorized Product By Employee",
  "sku": "UNAUTH-SKU-999",
  "description": "This should be forbidden with 403",
  "purchasePrice": 10.00,
  "salePrice": 20.00,
  "stockMinimo": 5
}

###

# 7.2 Employee attempts to create a purchase order (Denied -> HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branchId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "supplier": "Unauthorized Supplier",
  "reference": "PO-FORBIDDEN-001"
}

###

# 7.3 Employee attempts to view owner-restricted sales summary (Denied -> HTTP 403 Forbidden)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/reports/sales/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

# 7.4 Employee attempts to create notification recipient (Denied -> HTTP 403 Forbidden)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/notifications/recipients
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unauthorized Recipient",
  "email": "intruder@stocksync.demo",
  "phone": "+573009999999",
  "preferredChannel": "Email"
}


### ==============================================================================
### SCENARIO 8: Invalid or Expired Token (Expected: HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
### Requirement: Demonstrate that a tampered, invalid, or expired JWT cannot access protected endpoints.
### ==============================================================================

# 8.1 Access with malformed/tampered JWT (HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.invalidpayloadsignaturetampered.xyz123
Accept: application/json

###

# 8.2 Access with simulated expired JWT (HTTP 401 Unauthorized)
# Token issued with expiration in the past (exp: 1514764800 -> Jan 1, 2018)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMTExMTExMS0xMTExLTExMTEtMTExMS0xMTExMTExMTExMTEiLCJleHAiOjE1MTQ3NjQ4MDB9.invalid
Accept: application/json
